title: note_subcaptain_riddle
---
Halyna kept me sane through every storm. Grisha will captain his own ship one day. Anya still waits for me on the dock.
===

title: note_c01
---
"Your calm is the first tool. Your obedience is the second."
<page>
In any emergency, report to ~your ~ S ~uperior~.
Trust him: he already knows ~this ~ o ~cean~ and its temper.
Doubting the chain of command is not caution. It is betrayal.
Getting lost at sea is an accident.
Losing ~your ~ S ~uperior's~ trust is a shipwreck you don't come back from.
<page>
*The radio hides the lies.*
===

title: note_c02
---
MAPA DE NAVEGACIÓN — EL MARINERA
Deck B: Zonas de habitabilidad y mando.
Deck C: Zonas técnicas y operativas.
El acceso a cada zona está regulado por su credencial de rango.
Las zonas sin señalización corresponden a sectores restringidos.
ZONA RESTRINGIDA: acceso exclusivo por autorización directa.
No solicite información sobre estas zonas a su superior.
===

title: note_c03
---
CONOCE TU ROL EN EL MARINERA
OVEJA — Tripulación general. Acceso: exterior, balcones, zonas comunes. Tu seguridad es nuestra prioridad.
CABALLO — Personal técnico. Acceso: salas de energía, sala de agua, corredores técnicos. Tu llave abre lo que necesitas. No lo que quieres.
PERRO — Seguridad y mando. Acceso: camarotes, comedor, zonas de seguridad. Tu función es mantener el orden. El orden te mantiene a ti.
CERDO — Dirección y ciencias. Acceso: laboratorio, consultorios, cubículos de mando. La misión del barco depende de tu trabajo. No lo interrumpas.
Cada rango tiene lo que necesita. Cada rango es necesario.
===

title: note_c04
---
Water is the blood that keeps this ship alive.
Keep it moving. Keep it clean. Keep it quiet.
===

title: note_c05
---
Power does not think — power obeys.
The current never rests, and neither should your loyalty.
===

title: note_c06
---
You are not individuals. You are the soul of El Marinera.
There is no soul without the ship.
===

title: note_d01
---
December 9th
Routine check done. The electricity room's mine to look after -- breaker panel, backup generator, wiring conduits. Everything read normal.
Bola de Nieve settled in fine at the Cat Room. Left him the old blanket and a bowl of water. Good cat. Doesn't bother anyone.
Today's rations tasted different. A bit metallic. Probably the preservatives in the new boxes. Not the first time they've switched suppliers without saying.
<page>
December 12th
Bola de Nieve's doing fine. Purrs when I come in. Good sign.
The water system in Deck C's corridors keeps making that noise. Already reported it twice. Nobody checks it. If it were a pressure leak it would've shown by now.
Rations came late today. The chef said there's an inventory problem. Didn't really follow the explanation. He looked uncomfortable when I asked.
The strange taste is still there. I'll get used to it.
<page>
December 20th
Something's off with Petrov. He used to be the most careful one on shift. Today he let a pressure reading slide that he would've logged three times before. Asked if he was okay. He looked at me like he didn't understand the question.
Wrote "switched off" in my observation notebook. Don't know how else to put it.
Bola de Nieve was restless this evening. Pacing in circles. Cats notice things.
Went up to the comms room to see if they could fix my handheld radio. Ended up staying a while, just listening to the guys work. There's something almost fun about Morse -- the way it sounds, the rhythm of it. Might actually learn it one of these days. Good way to hide a message, these days.
===

title: note_d02
---
25 de diciembre
Bola de Nieve no está en el Cat Room.
Revisé el sector completo. La manta está. El plato está. Él no está.
Alguien lo sacó. No hay otra explicación. La puerta del Cat Room tiene cerradura y solo los Caballos tenemos acceso. Eso reduce las posibilidades.
Lo encontraré.
Feliz navidad.
<page>
28 de diciembre
Estaba buscando a Bola de Nieve en los corredores de Deck C cuando noté algo.
Hay personas que no están apagadas como Petrov y los otros. Se mueven diferente. Hablan normal. Uno de ellos tiene credencial de Cerdo y come en otro lugar, no en el comedor general.
La diferencia es la comida. Tiene que serlo.
Los que comen del comedor cambian. Los que no comen del comedor no cambian.
Tengo que entender qué hay en las raciones.
<page>
1 de enero
Intenté llegar al Lab HallWay. Hay una puerta con lector negro. Mi credencial roja no funciona. Solo funciona en las zonas técnicas, como siempre.
No es justo que haya puertas que nadie explica. Tengo derecho a saber qué está pasando en mi barco.
Dejé comida extra en el Cat Room por si Bola de Nieve vuelve. Tal vez se fue él solo y encontró otro camino.
Año nuevo. El mismo barco.
===

title: note_d03
---
3 de enero
No dormí bien.
Esta mañana vi a alguien en el corredor C-2 usar una tarjeta negra en una puerta que no figura en los planos de mantenimiento. Una puerta que, según los planos, es pared.
Esperé cuarenta minutos en el corredor. Cuando salió, la tarjeta seguía en el bolsillo de su bata. Blanca. Era un Cerdo.
Hay puertas que no existen en los planos. Hay puertas que sí existen.
<page>
5 de enero
Tengo la tarjeta.
Sé que no debería haberla tomado pero a veces uno tiene que actuar aunque el reglamento diga lo contrario porque el reglamento no sabe lo que está pasando aquí y yo sí lo sé o casi lo sé y por eso tomé la tarjeta y la escondí bajo la manta de Bola de Nieve en el Cat Room donde nadie mirará porque nadie sabe que el gato es mío.
Mañana la uso. O pasado. Cuando sea el momento.
<page>
6 de enero
Los vi entrar.
Científicos. Batas blancas. Entraron al Lab HallWay por la puerta que no existe en los planos. Tres de ellos. Uno cargaba algo.
Hay algo detrás de esa pared que no es parte del barco que conozco.
Tengo la tarjeta.
Mañana entro.
===

title: note_d04
---
Sin fecha
Entré.
Vi lo que hay detrás.
No sé cómo escribirlo. No tengo las palabras para lo que vi y las palabras que tengo no encajan con lo que recuerdo y recuerdo fragmentos no todo lo que pasó adentro pero lo que recuerdo es suficiente para saber que
Voy primero al Cat Room.
Bola de Nieve tiene que estar ahí.
Después vuelvo y escribo todo.
===

title: note_d05
---
December 11th.
Quick log: the electricity machine isn't working right.
The first row of switches won't light up, but that doesn't bother me — I already know the password.
What I need to remember is that the second and third rows, together, have to match the first.
===

title: note_l01
---
REGISTRO DE OBSERVACIÓN — SUJETO KRK-01 — Sesión 01 — 18 de noviembre
Evaluación inicial completada.
Línea base establecida: lógica 94%, coordinación motora 91%, tolerancia al estrés 87%.
Primera dosis administrada: 0.3ml solución KRK-NL estándar.
Sin efectos observables en las primeras seis horas.
El sujeto cooperó sin resistencia. Primera respuesta documentable esperada en 72-96 horas.
Estado general: óptimo.
<page>
REGISTRO DE OBSERVACIÓN — SUJETO KRK-01 — Sesión 03 — 24 de noviembre
Primera mejora documentada.
El sujeto presenta reducción notable de respuestas reactivas. Comunicación más directa, menos elaborada. Obedece instrucciones sin demora ni cuestionamiento.
Apetito aumentado: solicita ración adicional al finalizar la sesión.
Conclusión: el programa está mostrando respuesta temprana positiva.
<page>
REGISTRO DE OBSERVACIÓN — SUJETO KRK-01 — Sesión 05 — 30 de noviembre
El vocabulario del sujeto se ha simplificado. Frases más cortas. Menor uso de subordinadas.
Lo atribuyo a fatiga acumulada de navegación.
Test de lógica: descenso de 94% a 78%. Tests manuales: 91% estable.
Descenso a considerar, aunque no alarmante. Se continuará con el protocolo sin modificaciones.
<page>
REGISTRO DE OBSERVACIÓN — SUJETO KRK-01 — Sesión 07 — 6 de diciembre
El sujeto consumió el almuerzo sin cubiertos. No pareció notar el cambio en su propio comportamiento.
Tests cognitivos: 31%. Tests manuales: 88%.
La disociación entre funciones cognitivas y motoras es notable.
Recomendación: continuar. Esta disociación es precisamente lo que el programa busca documentar.
<page>
REGISTRO DE OBSERVACIÓN — SUJETO KRK-01 — Sesión 09 — 12 de diciembre
El sujeto rechaza la ración estándar. Solo acepta el concentrado proteico de la bandeja B.
No comprendo el mecanismo detrás de esta preferencia. Podría ser olfativa, podría ser conductual. No está en la literatura.
Para no interrumpir las observaciones, ajusté la dieta del sujeto a su preferencia.
La ciencia requiere adaptación.
<page>
REGISTRO DE OBSERVACIÓN — SUJETO KRK-01 — Sesión 11 — sin fecha
El sujeto ya no puede completar tests cognitivos. No responde a preguntas verbales. Solo reacciona ante la presencia de comida.
Durante la sesión de hoy se posicionó detrás de mí y permaneció ahí durante cuarenta minutos. No hizo nada. Solo esperó.
He decidido no volver a retrasar la ración al inicio de la sesión.
<page>
REGISTRO DE OBSERVACIÓN — SUJETO KRK-01 — Sesión 12 — sin fecha
El sujeto me atacó al entrar sin ración.
Hay una herida en el antebrazo derecho. Superficial.
No lo voy a reportar. Fue un error de protocolo mío: entré sin la ración estándar. No volverá a ocurrir.
El sujeto no tiene la culpa.
<page>
REGISTRO DE OBSERVACIÓN — SUJETO KRK-01 — Sesión 13 — sin fecha
El sujeto rechaza también el concentrado proteico.
Permanece en la esquina noreste de la sala. Mirando la pared.
No reacciona a la presencia de comida. No reacciona a mi presencia.
He salido de la sala.
No tengo más observaciones que registrar hoy.
===

title: note_l02
---
NOTA DE CIERRE — REGISTRO KRK-01
El encargado de este registro fue encontrado en la Sala de Observación el 23 de diciembre.
El sujeto KRK-01 estaba presente en la sala.
No se requieren más registros de este sujeto.
El programa continúa con otros sujetos.
===

title: note_t01
---
My love,
Writing this real late, everybody's asleep already but I can't get my eyes to close tonight.
Chef found some boxes down in the storeroom today. Army rations, still sealed, date on 'em is way off yet. We ate good tonight, first time in a long while. Real meat. Bread still warm out the oven.
Made me think somebody's looking out for us out here. Somebody up top knows we exist, at least.
Dmitri says the food tastes off. Told him it's just 'cause we ain't used to eating this good no more.
<page>
Portions were smaller today though.
Chef says it's gotta be that way, needs to last us. Nobody asked him how long for.
Me and Voronin walked out the mess hall and just looked at each other, didn't say nothing. Don't know why that stuck with me the way it did. Guess it was the first sign, I just didn't know it yet.
Miss you. Write back when you can.
===

title: note_t02
---
Somebody got into the cabin and took the stash I had under the bunk.
Only two people it could've been. Been bunking with 'em for months now.
Not saying nothing. Ain't no use saying nothing.
From now on I'm keeping what's left somewhere else.
===

title: note_t03
---
Aleksei stopped talking.
Used to tell stories in the mess hall about his daughter. Said she was turning five. Said he promised her a dog.
Now he just comes in, eats fast, and leaves.
Guess it's the hunger. Does something different to each of us.
===

title: note_t04
---
Repin and Zakharov got into it in the mess hall today.
Came aboard together. Used to be friends.
Over the last portion off the center plate. The one nobody touches 'cause it's supposed to be for everyone.
Nobody stepped in. Nobody said a word.
After that they ate on opposite ends of the table. Like the other one wasn't even there. Like they'd never been friends at all.
===

title: note_t05
---
I eat facing the wall now.
So nobody sees how much I've got left.
I know Dobrovolsky watches my plate. Caught him at it. Started noticing it about three days ago.
Don't know when I started caring more about what's on my plate than the person sitting across from me.
Guess it happened gradual.
===

title: note_t06
---
Mirov stopped coming to the mess hall.
Found him this morning in corridor B-3, just standing there facing the wall. Not doing anything. Just standing.
Talked to him. He looked at me.
His eyes were wrong somehow. Like he was seeing me but not looking at what I was.
Went to the mess hall alone.
===

title: note_t07
---
i'm hungry
today's ration wasn't enough
i don't understand why i'm so hungry if i ate
i'm hungry
===

title: note_v01
---
Okay... I don't really know why I'm recording this. I just need to say it out loud, I think.
Adrian is interesting. Genuinely. The way he talks, it's — I don't know, I could just sit there and listen to him for hours. Charming isn't even the word for it.
The ship scared me, before. All of it, the size, the sound it makes at night. But being near him... I don't feel calmer. If anything I feel more on edge. Like something's off.
<page>
It's been a few days now, and I keep getting this feeling that there's more than one of him. Like there's the Adrian who's talking to me, and then there's someone else underneath that I haven't met yet.
He says he's the chef, but he's barely ever in the kitchen. He's in his room. Always in his room.
And when I can, when he's not looking, I peek at his notes. They don't look like recipes. They look like chemistry. I don't know anything about chemistry, but I know what a recipe looks like, and that's not it.
Something's wrong here. I don't like it. And I really don't like being kept in the dark.
===

title: note_v02
---
Okay— the storm. That storm that hit us two nights ago, I'm still kind of shaking just thinking about it. The whole ship was creaking, I mean really creaking, like it was gonna come apart underneath us.
And Adrian... nothing. Didn't check on me, didn't say a word. Which, fine, whatever, but it's not just that night. He talks to me less every day now. I ask him something and I get, like, three words back. I don't know if he's busy or if he's just done with me, and it bothers me more than I want to admit.
<page>
So I did something about it. I started talking to the sub-captain. A lot. Flirting, honestly — men are easy to fool when they see some good curves, so I figured, if Adrian's not gonna tell me anything, maybe he will.
And it worked. Better than I thought, actually. He let a few things slip — small things, but enough. Enough that I'm almost sure the two of them know something they're not sharing.
<page>
I have a plan. I'm not gonna pretend it's the most... ethical thing I've ever done, but I'm tired. Tired of being ignored, tired of being the last one to know anything on this ship. If this is what it takes to get Adrian to actually look at me again, then fine.
...I wonder what Mom would think of me right now.
===

title: note_v03
---
Entré al laboratorio.
Adrian no es lo que dijo ser. Eso lo sabía. Ahora sé qué es.
Encontré los registros. Encontré la variante. La diferencia entre KRK-NL estándar y la variante reptiliana es una cuestión de umbral. La estándar borra. La variante transforma.
La confrontación tiene que ser ahora. Antes de que él decida que soy un problema que hay que resolver.
La única palanca que me queda es lo que encontré en ese laboratorio. La única palanca que me queda soy yo.
Mamá tenía diecisiete años cuando tomó la primera decisión que la definió para siempre. Yo tengo veinticuatro.
===

title: note_a01
---
Okay — the mess hall. People are in there constantly, and they actually talk, I mean real conversation, like there's trust between them. Guard's completely down.
Except when someone with a Dog rank walks in. Then the tone shifts, just like that, every time.
This whole rank system, it's... curious, I'll say that much. But everyone treats it like it's just how things work here, so I'm not gonna waste time picking at it. Not yet anyway.
Crew's mostly Russian, a few Ukrainians, one Belarusian. None of them trained for this. Easy to read.
<page>
I met a woman. Let her come aboard with me.
She's pretty, sure. But she talks — a lot, more than I need her to.
I didn't bring her up here for conversation.
<page>
Most nights I go prepare something in the kitchen. That's... that's the phrase I use for it. Works well enough.
<page>
Vanessa's asked me twice now why I go out at night. Like there's some other woman on this ship I'd be sneaking off to see.
Gets old. Fast, some days.
===

title: note_a02
---
The supplies — they're gone. Destroyed. First I figured it was the storm, made sense given the timing. But the more I look at it, the less that story holds together.
It was Vanessa. Has to be.
Last time we talked she started something. A real scene, in front of people, trying to get the crew on her side. And of course some of them jumped right in — the Pigs, mostly. Wasn't hard to see coming. Funny what some men will do for a woman.
<page>
Had to do something. We can't make port, not now, not with everything else in motion.
Found some MERI rations I'd set aside earlier. Not great stuff, I know that. So I added... something. A little help, let's call it that. Nothing anyone needs the details on.
<page>
Few days in and it's working. People stopped complaining about the taste. Back to work, functioning normally.
More docile than before, maybe. But they're compliant. That's what matters right now.
<page>
Vanessa's getting more dangerous by the day. She's talking to everyone now. Even found out she's sleeping with the Captain.
Bothers me, I won't pretend it doesn't. But it doesn't matter, not really.
Talked to him — asked him to keep an eye on her. Told him I think she's up to something.
===

title: note_a03
---
20 de diciembre: primer incidente en el corredor B-2. Dos tripulantes. Resuelto.
21: segundo incidente. Comedor. Resuelto.
23: tercer incidente. No resuelto.
24: cuatro incidentes.
26: perdí la cuenta.
Algo en las dosis o en la duración salió de los parámetros documentados.
La misión de contención se está escapando de las manos.
Lo que tengo que hacer ahora es recuperar el control del laboratorio antes de que alguien de afuera decida hacerlo por mí.
===

title: note_a04
---
No time to explain this properly, I just need to get it out.
The mission's compromised. Before I go down, I need the doll from the clock's drawer — code's the three vowels in my own name, should've picked something I don't have to think this hard to remember right now.
I have to get back to the lab, grab the USB, and run Protocol SCUTTLE before anyone finds that hallway. Twelve minutes, maybe less if the vents are clear. After that the kitchen stays sealed. Nobody goes back in.
<page>
And of course, now, of all times, I can't find the key to my case. Not on the desk. Not in the drawer. I've checked twice.
Vanessa. I don't want it to be her. But it has to be her.
Without that key I can't get back into the kitchen at all. She didn't just take a key. She bought herself time, and I still don't know what she's planning to do with it.
===

title: note_b01
---
CIA TECHNICAL SERVICES DIVISION — FIELD SIGNAL UNIT "BEEPER" — OPERATOR CARD
CLASSIFICATION: RESTRICTED

PURPOSE
Short-range audible relay for a pre-arranged three-letter authentication code. Standard International Morse. No radio signature, no paper trail — just sound, and only for whoever is close enough and built to listen for it.
<page>
OPERATION
1. Hold INPUT to key a DASH. Tap INPUT to key a DOT.
2. Three seconds without input locks the current letter and opens the next.
3. Repeat until all three letters of your code are set.
4. Press OUTPUT to transmit. Any unit within range keyed to that exact code will register it.
A wrong code transmits — it simply answers nothing. The unit will not tell you which letter missed.
<page>
SECURITY NOTICE
The code is worthless without this unit. This unit is worthless without the code. Never record, carry, or store the two together.
Losing one half is an inconvenience. Losing both is a compromised operation.
Report the loss of either immediately.
===
